A||||7||gtsonly||top end off help- please?????????||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||10-25-2001||09:49 PM||||With the top end off (in Car) cam exposed, can I spray a cleaner to remove sludge and carbon without hurting the cam or bearings? This would drain into the oil pan where I could clean later. Can this be done?<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-26-2001||01:07 PM||||I don't know if this is the "right" way or not, but here's what Stu did:  Carefully chip away at hardened oil desposits, while running a shop vac (keeping the hose near where you're cleaning) to snatch all the chunks of stuff before they can fall into the pan.<P>A few little crumbs will probably escape into the pan. Blow compressed air onto the cam, to knock off any escapees that landed there.  They will end up in the pan, too.  Oh, well.  Let the oil filter get them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||10-26-2001||09:37 PM||||Hey Chris, Hows it going?? We miss you up this way. I would just go with what StuGood said. I don't think it would be good to use any type of cleaning solvent.<P>You would not know my car now. It is not the ratty ride it was when you were were around here. What do you think?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/im7.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Lucky4_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Lucky3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Lucky6_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/battl.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/im3.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||theogre||10-27-2001||01:39 PM||||The cleaning likely won't hurt the cam. Avoid spraying it with anything that could drive dirt into the bearings. plug the lifter bores with rag to keep trash out.<P>You need to get it oiled back up after cleaning or you'll tear it up really quick. <P>If you use a shop vac, do it out side and only if you have NOT used cleaning solvents. Shop vac motors aren't explosion proof and could ignite fumes if they become concentrated enough.<P>After you finish cleaning drench everything with fresh motor oil and let it drain away. Then drian the oil pan and put in fresh oil before starting the engine.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||recluse||10-27-2001||01:55 PM||||88coupeV6....  nice car.<BR>what did you use to make the console black?<BR>and also, did you use a mounting kit to mount the battery up front or just make a way to do it yourself, and do you have to remove it to get the spare out?  <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||10-27-2001||02:02 PM||||When I did my topend I shop vac'd like Stu did and did as Ogre mentioned with an additional step before the oil drenching.  I got a gallon of diesel and carefully rinsed as much as I could to the pan from the lifter galley on my V6.  I had the oil pan drain plug off and a catch pan underneath.  This method rinsed a lot of crap from the engine as caught in the pan.  When I started running it after assembly, I changed the oil at 100 miles but not the filter.  My Oil pressure is 65 lbs at cruise when hot (and I mean hot) and 25 lbs at idle.  GL||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||10-28-2001||08:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR><B>88coupeV6....  nice car.<BR>what did you use to make the console black?<BR>and also, did you use a mounting kit to mount the battery up front or just make a way to do it yourself, and do you have to remove it to get the spare out?  <BR>thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, I used an interior spray dye. I got it from JC Whitney. I mounted the battery by flipping the spare upside down and putting the optima battery inside. I then just used the stock Tire holddown around the battery/tire. Yes you would have to remove the battery to get the spare out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hope that helps<P>||||reg||7
Z||000007||gtsonly||10-28-2001||07:29 PM||||thanks all for the advice, I hope to have the car back on the road by the end of november, just in time to put it up for the winter. I miss the guys from Massachusetts. Thats a great group of people up there. <P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||10
